# tools/p/prose_register_witness.rish -- prose that measures, measured.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. On 20260823 Keaton read a freshly written front door, labelled Radiant, and said
# it was the opposite of the intention. Counting agreed: 46% of README sentences and 54% of a
# founding statement's carried a negative, against 29% in RADIANT_STYLE.md itself -- a founding
# statement twice as negative as the guide it claimed to follow. The reading grade sat inside
# target the whole time, which is exactly why nobody caught it, and why a syllable count was never
# going to.
#
# The meter that already stood, tools/fixtures/r/radiant_negation_scan.sh, counts NEGATION WORDS
# across `.claude/rules/*.md` alone. Two honest gaps: the front door was never on its roster, and
# negative FRAMING -- fails, broken, lost, refused, stale, problem -- went uncounted. The two
# meters are siblings rather than rivals: one guards the rules, this one guards the door.
#
# Both documents were rewritten the same day, to 15% and 11%, and this rung keeps them there.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   Every document on the DOOR roster keeps its negative-sentence share at or under 20%. Five
#   stand there as of 20260823.061415: the front door, the foundations index, the founding
#   statement, and -- swept onto it that day -- the beginner tutorial and the demos page, a
#   newcomer's second and third click. The roster is named rather than discovered, so a new file
#   joins the enforced tier by a hand rather than by accident.
#   Fifteen behaviors on planted prose, using the scan's own measure function lifted verbatim so
#   the control reads exactly what the guard reads: warm prose low, refusal-led prose high, the two
#   discriminated, fenced code excluded, tables and headings read past, fragments under four words
#   skipped, an empty page safe, and the live door roster clean.
#   Six of the fifteen arrived with REDS %451, and each refuses under the elder reading and passes
#   under this one -- a case green both ways proves nothing. A paragraph opening with a bold span is
#   read, where `/^[ \t]*[-*>#]/` dropped every one of them; a real bullet is still read past, the
#   marker THEN whitespace, which also catches the `+` bullet that class never held at all; front
#   matter is dropped ON PURPOSE, its wrapped value riding to the blank line, which is what finally
#   drops the shared `**Where this sits:**` navigation block; and the two refusal legs prove the
#   head rule stops there -- a bold lead-in AFTER the front matter is prose, and a bold opening that
#   carries no short key is prose too. Shape alone ate real text on 77 of 703 living documents when
#   it was tried, so position and shape are both required.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED, as a ratchet under a ceiling that only ever falls FOR A GIVEN READING. The
# teaching tier -- docs-geode/, manual/, docs-geode/edu/yonder/, and the root guides -- counted as documents above the
# Field target of 30%. Sixteen at seating, the beginner tutorial itself at 51% and the demos page at
# 62%; fourteen after the first sweep lap carried those two to 0% and 15%; zero by 20260823.070754.
# RE-SEATED at 5 on 20260906, when measure() began reading the body paragraphs the elder `*` branch
# dropped. The five are named in the scan beside the ceiling, with both readings and both sentence
# counts, so a lane sweeping one takes its name off and the number falls. None of the five got
# worse -- each has read over the Field target the whole time, on the half of itself the meter could
# not see.
#
# THE BLIND SPOT IS COUNTED NOW, rather than written into a header once. The scan reads every
# tracked README.md -- `tools/fixtures/` and `vendor/` read past, since a frozen plant and
# third-party source are pages no lane may sweep -- holds each to the same eight-sentence floor,
# and prints `front_doors`, `front_doors_readable`, `front_doors_unrostered_over` and a
# `candidate:` line naming each door the roster leaves out that stands above the ceiling. So the
# green says THE DOORS THAT AGREED ARE INSIDE and shows its work. The reading is REPORTED and
# never gated, proven in a pen: one over-ceiling page off the roster is named and the verdict
# still reads ok; the same bytes on the roster refuse at `door_over_ceiling=1`. One roster line
# apart, so the report is told from the gate rather than assumed to differ from it.
#
# THE LAW ROOM READS ITS OWN NUMBER NOW, from 20260910. The header above hands `.claude/rules/*.md`
# to a sibling, and the sibling stands -- tools/fixtures/r/radiant_negation_scan.sh is rostered and
# enforcing over exactly those files. It reads a DIFFERENT number: negation WORDS per file against
# that file's own 20260821 baseline, which is a ratchet with no floor. A law page may sit at 63%
# negative sentences forever and stay green, provided it never reads worse than the day somebody
# measured it. So the room that teaches the register had never been compared against the ceiling
# context/GAUGE_STYLE.md writes down, in the eighteen days both meters ran side by side.
#
# Measured on the seating lap: 54 pages, 38 clearing the eight-sentence floor, and 18 of the 38
# above the Field target of 30% at the writing, 19 on the commit that shipped after a peer's lap
# landed one more -- azimuth-galaxy-proposal-format 63% of 11 sentences,
# comlink-tendency 58% of 12, git-signing 55% of 58, the-baton 46% of 86. The law room runs the
# most negative prose this meter reads. Field rather than Door because Gauge seats Meter for ledger
# rows, witness headers and commit bodies alone, and a rule page is documentation addressed to a
# working agent; whether the room should be held tighter is Keaton's word, and Field costs it
# nothing. The tier GATES under a ceiling that only falls, beside the teaching tier, since these
# are living Tier 3 pages a lane repairs one at a time.
#
# Five behaviors prove it in a pen carrying its own DOOR roster: the cold page is named by path
# and share, the warm page written the same day in the same room stays off the listing, a page
# under the eight-sentence floor is unread rather than counted, one page over a ceiling of zero
# refuses, and the same bytes at a ceiling of one walk free. Two scan mutations bite -- dropping
# the gate clause, and dropping the target comparison.
#
# AND THE TEACHING CEILING FELL 5 TO 4 in the same commit, giving back a slot that was never a
# page. The five named in the scan include one that sits under the eight-sentence floor, so the
# reading has answered 4 since the day the ceiling was seated at 5 by counting the prose list
# rather than by asking the meter.
#
# A SHARE NAMES A PAGE; --explain NAMES THE SENTENCES, from 20260910. Every tier here printed a
# document and its share and stopped -- `law: .claude/rules/git-signing.md 55% (32 of 58 sentences)`
# -- so a lane told that thirty-two sentences carry a negative had to find them by reading, and the
# finding is most of what a register sweep costs. `sh tools/fixtures/p/prose_register_scan.sh
# --explain <path>` prints each counted sentence with the words that counted it. It is a MODE rather
# than a second tool, calling the same measure() with one flag set, so the listing agrees with the
# gate's number by construction rather than by care.
#
# Nine behaviors prove it in a pen: the rows exist, one row per counted negative, the word named,
# capitals kept, the row aligned to the sentence that carried the word, a warm page listing nothing,
# the listing bounded and saying where it stopped, an absent path refused, and measure() answering
# the same three numbers with the flag as without it. Two mutations bite -- dropping the
# substitutions from the second buffer misprints two rows of five, and dropping the bound prints
# past it in silence.
#
# THE SECOND BUFFER IS WHY THE ROWS READ TRUE. The reading buffer is lowercased with links and code
# spans replaced, and `**wrong.**` holds a period the splitter reaches only once the emphasis marks
# come off. So the file's own bytes split differently from the buffer the meter counts -- by four to
# fourteen sentences on nearly every page in the law room and the foundations -- and a listing built
# from them would name a warm sentence as negative. The mode carries a parallel buffer with the same
# substitutions and its capitals kept, split by the same delimiter at the same offsets.
#
# THE CEILING FELL 19 -> 17 the day the mode landed, on the two pages it was pointed at first:
# comlink-tendency 58% of 12 sentences and azimuth-galaxy-proposal-format 63% of 11, both to 0%,
# seven counted sentences each restated and every claim, name, path and stamp held. It fell 17 -> 14
# 14 -> 9 on 20260910.150347, the five pages the listing priced at one or two counted sentences
# each -- tame-guidance, placeholder-ship-names, remember, remember-git-nib, session-log-provenance,
# nine counted words between them and every claim, path and stamp held. It fell 17 -> 14
# the same day on the three pages the listing priced at ONE restatement each -- molt 35% of 14,
# vocabulary-aroma 32% of 25, exec-bit 31% of 32, all three reading 28% after one counted word
# apiece went. Reading the room cheapest-first is what the mode made possible.
#
# EVERY LEG OF THE PEN IS HEARD, and until `20260910.125644` only the named ones were. The control
# ended on `control_verdict=ok`, which says it reached its own last line and nothing about what its
# legs read, so a leg could answer `no` under a GREEN gate. Measured on the seating lap: all 32 legs
# standing that day were in fact asserted by name below, so the hole was the leg a lap opens
# tomorrow. `say()` in the control tallies `control_legs` and `control_failed`, derived from the
# legs themselves rather than typed here, and both are asserted -- the floor beneath the named
# assertions, each of which still carries the sentence a reader repairs by. Two mutations bite: one
# leg flipped to refuse reads `control_failed=1`, and a leg added with no assertion of its own moves
# `control_legs` to 33. The readings are untouched, proven rather than claimed -- the control's whole
# output before the change is byte-identical to its output after, minus the two new lines. This is
# the third room to close the shape, after the ascii pen and Patchouli's `silent_leg`.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That the prose is GOOD. This counts negation density, one honest proxy among
# several. A page can pass this meter and still fail a reader, so the second number to read is
# always the prose itself.
#
# Style: context/GAUGE_STYLE.md - Rule: .claude/rules/gauge-style.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/p/prose_register_witness.rish

say "prose-register: Language EN -- a style label nobody measures is a wish, and this tree wished for months."
say "prose-register: Style Gauge -- the door setting, held at a number rather than at an intention."
say "prose-register: Lens TAME -- safety first: the front door is what a stranger meets, and it was the least measured page we own."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/prose_register_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "prose-register: a door document reads more negatively than the style it claims"
assert scan.out contains "door_over_ceiling=0" else "prose-register: every door document must hold at or under 20% negative sentences"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "prose-register: the scan must balance before it is believed"
assert scan.out contains "law_ceiling=9" else "prose-register: the law tier ceiling only ever falls -- lower it in the commit that sweeps a rule page"
say "field GREEN -- the front door reads the way the style says it does, and the law room now reads its own number"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/prose_register_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "prose-register: the control must complete"
assert control.out contains "warm_reads_low=yes" else "prose-register: affirmative prose must measure low"
assert control.out contains "cold_reads_high=yes" else "prose-register: refusal-led prose must measure high"
assert control.out contains "reading_discriminates=yes" else "prose-register: the reading must tell the two apart, or it measures nothing"
assert control.out contains "fence_excluded=yes" else "prose-register: a fenced code block is code, and must not colour the reading"
assert control.out contains "table_excluded=yes" else "prose-register: tables and headings carry labels rather than sentences"
assert control.out contains "fragments_skipped=yes" else "prose-register: a fragment under four words is no sentence"
assert control.out contains "empty_safe=yes" else "prose-register: an empty page must read zero rather than divide by zero"
assert control.out contains "bold_lead_is_read=yes" else "prose-register: a paragraph opening with a bold span is prose, and must be read"
assert control.out contains "bold_lead_reads_high=yes" else "prose-register: reading a bold-led paragraph must change the share it measures"
assert control.out contains "bullets_excluded=yes" else "prose-register: a real bullet -- the marker then whitespace -- must still be read past"
assert control.out contains "front_matter_excluded=yes" else "prose-register: front matter and its wrapped value must be dropped on purpose"
assert control.out contains "body_after_front_matter_is_read=yes" else "prose-register: the head rule must stop at the blank line, or it eats Gauge's own lead-ins"
assert control.out contains "bold_opening_without_key_is_read=yes" else "prose-register: a bold opening carrying no short key is a sentence"
assert control.out contains "live_door_clean=yes" else "prose-register: the live door roster must agree with the control's reading"
assert control.out contains "live_verdict_ok=yes" else "prose-register: the scan must agree with itself"
assert control.out contains "census_names_the_page=yes" else "prose-register: the unrostered census must name the page by path and share, or a count nobody can act on is all it prints"
assert control.out contains "census_reported_not_gated=yes" else "prose-register: a front door that agreed to nothing must be reported and never refuse the tree"
assert control.out contains "census_roster_gates_the_same_page=yes" else "prose-register: the same page one roster line apart must refuse, or the reading cannot be told from the gate"
assert control.out contains "law_names_the_page=yes" else "prose-register: the law tier must name an over-target rule page by path and share"
assert control.out contains "law_spares_the_warm_page=yes" else "prose-register: a warm rule page must stay off the listing, or the tier counts every rule it finds"
assert control.out contains "law_floor_holds=yes" else "prose-register: a rule page under the eight-sentence floor must be unread rather than counted"
assert control.out contains "law_ceiling_refuses=yes" else "prose-register: one law page over the ceiling must refuse, or the tier gates nothing"
assert control.out contains "law_ceiling_lifts=yes" else "prose-register: the same bytes one ceiling number apart must walk free, or the refusal cannot be told from a scan that refuses everything"
assert control.out contains "explain_names_the_sentences=yes" else "prose-register: --explain must name the sentences a share counts, or a lane sweeping the page is guessing"
assert control.out contains "explain_agrees_with_the_count=yes" else "prose-register: one listed row per counted negative -- a listing that disagrees with its own gate is worse than none"
assert control.out contains "explain_names_the_word=yes" else "prose-register: the row must name the word that counted the sentence"
assert control.out contains "explain_keeps_capitals=yes" else "prose-register: the printed sentence must keep its capitals, or a lane cannot find it in the file"
assert control.out contains "explain_aligns_after_normalising=yes" else "prose-register: the printed sentence must be the sentence that carried the word, past emphasis marks and links"
assert control.out contains "explain_warm_lists_nothing=yes" else "prose-register: a warm page must list nothing and still answer"
assert control.out contains "explain_bounded=yes" else "prose-register: the listing is an allocation -- bound it, and say where it stopped"
assert control.out contains "explain_refuses_an_absent_path=yes" else "prose-register: an absent path must refuse rather than read as a clean page"
assert control.out contains "explain_reading_unchanged=yes" else "prose-register: --explain must add a printout and move no number the gate reads"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "prose-register: the control must agree with itself"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "prose-register: a leg of the pen read no -- run sh tools/fixtures/p/prose_register_control.sh and read the =no lines"
assert control.out contains "control_legs=32" else "prose-register: the pen's leg count moved -- raise it when a leg lands, and never lower it to make a deletion quiet"
say "the reading discriminates -- warm prose low, refusal-led prose high, and the edges read correctly"

say "GREEN: prose-register -- prose that measures, measured."
